Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||02-22-2001||08:52 PM||||Has anyone stuck a 318 Mopar in a fiero?<BR>I had a 73 Charger and loved the 318.<P>I was just wondering if anyone has wondered down this path.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jake_Dragon<BR>1985 2.5L Sport Coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/rebel33/fiero.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-23-2001||11:10 AM||||the 318 is pretty much bulletproof. but since youde be changing from a gm its gonna be lots harder, wiring and everything would be incompatable. Youll have to fabricate all your own mounts, exhaust, cooling system hookups. Any thing can be done if you really want it. I used to be a die hard Mopar fan and if i was going to do a swap, Id forget the 318 and go for the really hot 340. Maybe even the six pack. The 340 will totally smoke any 318. That what knocked Camaro and Mustangs off their high horses.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gabriel||02-23-2001||02:29 PM||||<BR>&gt;That what knocked Camaro and Mustangs off their high horses.<P>    Not in my nieghborhood Rog ...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Actually the 340 is/was a nice freaking setup.  Way better than the Al Bundy 318 Duster thing.  I paid more care with the 340 Cuda than the 396 Chevelle. <P>||||reg||1
